        "body": {
          "en": "Non-routine geometry questions involve multiple theorems applied together — circle inscribed in a triangle, overlapping regions, and proof-based reasoning.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inscribed angle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{1}{2}\\times \\) central angle",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power of a point",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( PA\\cdot PB=PC\\cdot PD \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Heron's formula",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Regular polygon area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{1}{4}ns^2\\cot(\\pi/n) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the area of a triangle with sides 7, 8, 9. \\[ s=12,\\quad A=\\sqrt{12\\cdot5\\cdot4\\cdot3}=\\sqrt{720}=12\\sqrt5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
