      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Circle Theorems & 3D Solids",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Key circle theorems: (1) Angle at centre = 2 × angle at circumference. (2) Angles in same segment are equal. (3) Opposite angles in cyclic quadrilateral sum to 180°. (4) Tangent ⊥ radius. Surface area of sphere: \\(4\\pi r^2\\); volume: \\(\\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\). Cone volume: \\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Circle theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "O is the centre of a circle. Angle \\(AOB = 140°\\). Find the angle \\(ACB\\) where \\(C\\) is on the major arc. <p>Angle at circumference on minor arc \\(= 140°/2 = 70°\\). \\(C\\) is on major arc, so \\(\\angle ACB = 180° - 70° = 110°\\) (opposite angles in cyclic quad sum to \\(180°\\)).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A cone has base radius 6 cm and slant height 10 cm. Find its total surface area.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Height: \\(h = \\sqrt{100-36} = 8\\) cm. TSA \\(= \\pi r^2 + \\pi r l = 36\\pi + 60\\pi = 96\\pi \\approx 301.6\\) cm\\(^2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
